/** \addtogroup testing_building
 * @{
 *
 * Build tests on demand (available even when `HCIREDUCE_BUILD_TESTS=OFF`):
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * cmake -S . -B _build
 * cmake --build _build --target tests -j
 * \endcode
 *
 * Configure tests as part of the default build and register them with CTest:
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * cmake -S . -B _build -DHCIREDUCE_BUILD_TESTS=ON
 * cmake --build _build -j
 * ctest --test-dir _build --output-on-failure
 * \endcode
 *
 * Build and run a single test source:
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * cmake -S . -B _build \
 *   -DHCIREDUCE_BUILD_TESTS=ON \
 *   -DHCIREDUCE_ONE_TEST=common/HCIobservation_test.cpp
 * cmake --build _build --target hcireduceTestOne -j
 * cmake --build _build --target hcireduceTestOneRun
 * \endcode
 *
 * Build the Doxygen documentation directly, or include it in the default build:
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * cmake --build _build --target docs
 * cmake -S . -B _build -DHCIREDUCE_BUILD_DOCS=ON
 * \endcode
 *
 * Coverage generation requires `lcov` and `genhtml`:
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * cmake -S . -B _build
 * cmake --build _build --target coverage
 * \endcode
 *
 * The coverage workflow configures an isolated instrumented build, runs its
 * CTest suite, and writes these artifacts beneath `_build/`:
 *
 * - `coverage.info`
 * - `coverage_filtered.info`
 * - `doc/html/coverage/index.html`
 * - `doc/html/index.html`
 *
 * Set `HCIREDUCE_COVERAGE_TEST_TIMEOUT` to change the default 300-second test
 * timeout. Clean generated reports and the isolated build with:
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * cmake --build _build --target coverage_clean
 * \endcode
 *
 * Convenience wrappers are available as `tests/coverage/make_coverage` and
 * `tests/coverage/update_coverage`.
 *
 * @}
 */
